# Deployed Python function bundle exclusions.
#
# The production API's lexical retrieval reads the PERSISTED bm25s index
# (data/bm25s_index/) at runtime -- see retrieval/lexical_backend.py and
# retrieval/bm25_search.py's get_index()/_select_backend(). It never reads
# the per-filing chunk JSONL files or raw filing artifacts directly.
#
# data/chunks/**/*_chunks.jsonl and data/raw/**/metadata.json are needed only
# by offline tooling (ingestion, scripts/build_bm25s_index.py, verify_company,
# evaluation scripts) and by the SEC_RAG_LEXICAL_BACKEND=current fallback
# mode, which production does not use. They stay in git for local dev,
# ingestion, and reproducibility, but are excluded from the deployed function
# bundle -- this was the direct cause of a Wave-1 deploy failure (bundle size
# 238.39 MB > Vercel's 225 MB Python function cap) even after Vercel's
# automatic dependency optimization.
#
# Keep data/bm25s_index/, data/registry/, and code deployed as before.
data/chunks/
data/raw/
data/sec_cache/
data/embeddings/
